ravi: Heads up — onboarding quickstart stuck on 'Initializing...' after I paste my API key and click Run. No error in the UI, just a spinner.

devex-bot: infra-check: quickstart sample container healthy. No 5xx in last 10m.

elsa: Can you run a curl from your terminal and paste the response? Also is that a user token or a service key?

ravi: curl output: `HTTP/1.1 402 Payment Required`
Body: `\{"error\":\"billing_required\",\"message\":\"Activate billing for workspace ws_ravi to make requests\"\}`
Browser console: `TypeError: Failed to fetch` and the spinner keeps spinning.

kai: 402 explains it — invited workspaces can land in billing-disabled state. The quickstart client is currently retrying on all failure categories, so it treats 4xx like transient network errors and retries forever. That leaves the UI in a perpetual 'Initializing' state.

elsa: Workarounds: 1) If you have admin rights, add a card in Org -> Billing. 2) Create a service key in Org -> API keys and use that in the quickstart. Service keys bypass the per-user billing gating for tests.

ravi: Confirmed: `curl -H 'Authorization: Bearer sk_service_test' https://api.redwood.ai/v1/responses -d '{\"input\":\"hi\"}'` -> 200 OK, sample returned response. Works with service key.

devex-bot: ticket created: DEVEX-450 "quickstart: stop infinite retry on 4xx and surface billing required modal"

kai: Plan: update sample client to treat 4xx as non-retriable and display an explicit billing modal when error.error === 'billing_required'. Example patch: ```js
const resp = await fetch(...);
if (!resp.ok) {
  const body = await resp.json().catch(() => ({}));
  if (resp.status >= 400 && resp.status < 500) {
    if (body.error === 'billing_required') { showBillingModal(body.message || 'Activate billing'); return; }
    showClientError(body.message || 'Request failed'); return;
  }
  // existing retry logic for 5xx/network
}
```

elsa: Also adding an SDK change to surface a BillingRequiredError so downstream apps don't have to parse status codes. Will add telemetry quickstart.billing_402 when this happens.

kai: Filing UX ticket UX-111 to ensure the console always surfaces a billing CTA for invited orgs when `billing_enabled` is false and role === 'admin'.

ravi: Thanks — switching to a service key unblocked me. Happy to validate the sample + SDK PRs.

elsa: Assigning kai + elsa to DEVEX-450. Will include a small e2e test to simulate 402 and verify modal appears (and that quickstart stops retrying).

kai: PRs: sample fix #5290, SDK error mapping #5291. Will loop in UX on UX-111. Thanks folks :raised_hands:
